; ⚠ THIS FILE WAS `control_inplace_ry_reject_state_prep.ll` — A DECLINE — UNTIL
; bd test_C_libtooling-drbq Inc 4, AND THE IR IS UNCHANGED. It is renamed rather
; than edited in place so the flip is visible in `git log --follow`, exactly as
; Inc 3 re-homed `control_inplace_ry_reject_in_loop.ll`. What its old header
; called "two things Inc 1 does not have" — the alloc hoisted with the gate, and
; a seed-identity fence on the merge φ's pred incoming — are precisely what this
; increment ships (F1 and `lowerRotations`' `!Chained` controlled arm).
;
; F2 IS VACUOUS HERE BY SHAPE, not by value: `icmp sgt` is not an equality, so no
; edge of this diamond PROVES `q == k` for any k, so no `-O1` fold can have
; replaced the arm's arg-0 by the condition register. That is why the ordered
; spelling is the one shape §14.11 Q1's owner option (b) would keep if the
; equality family were ever withdrawn.
